WEBVTT

00:00:04.422 --> 00:00:06.591
Where's the Silvius' crew?

00:00:06.841 --> 00:00:09.969
I'm sorry. I don't know.

00:00:10.219 --> 00:00:15.391
The Silvius did make it out of there
after helping you escape, though.

00:00:15.641 --> 00:00:17.476
That's a relief!

00:00:21.272 --> 00:00:22.315
Thanks.

00:00:22.565 --> 00:00:24.025
What amazing wheat!

00:00:24.275 --> 00:00:27.653
This little one must've come along
because it was worried about you!

00:00:27.904 --> 00:00:29.405
Yes.

00:00:34.035 --> 00:00:37.663
Luscinia is afraid of our Exile.

00:00:37.914 --> 00:00:41.125
That's why he wants Alvis, its "key"...

00:00:41.209 --> 00:00:47.798
<i>No matter what might await us there</i>

00:00:48.049 --> 00:00:56.474
<i>I'll go to unexplored territory with you</i>

00:01:04.732 --> 00:01:12.782
<i>I just had a short dream</i>

00:01:13.032 --> 00:01:17.411
<i>In it, I saw your back</i>

00:01:17.662 --> 00:01:23.584
<i>Was it the past? The future?</i>

00:01:23.834 --> 00:01:34.345
<i>Ignore the needle on that meter
pointing to the red zone</i>

00:01:34.595 --> 00:01:37.473
<i>And go where the tailwinds
and your feelings point you</i>

00:01:37.723 --> 00:01:43.646
<i>Every time I flap my wings, it makes me realize</i>

00:01:43.896 --> 00:01:49.193
<i>That there are skies
I'll never be able to see again</i>

00:01:49.443 --> 00:01:54.699
<i>But if you still want to take flight</i>

00:01:54.949 --> 00:02:01.497
<i>Then I will be your wings</i>

00:02:21.642 --> 00:02:27.231
This is Millia's, and this is Alvis and Dio's...

00:02:27.481 --> 00:02:31.235
Millia hasn't eaten much lately.

00:02:31.485 --> 00:02:33.321
I hope she'll be all right...

00:02:33.571 --> 00:02:35.114
Yeah.

00:02:37.116 --> 00:02:39.201
This is General (_)rang.

00:02:39.452 --> 00:02:44.206
He contributed greatly to
our victory in the last battle.

00:02:44.457 --> 00:02:46.751
<i>The Federation's 3rd Fleet...</i>

00:02:47.001 --> 00:02:51.047
This is Princess Millia,
the acting royal representative of Turan.

00:02:51.297 --> 00:02:53.215
My sincerest apologies.

00:02:53.466 --> 00:02:57.178
What was done to your family
and your people was reprehensible.

00:02:58.471 --> 00:03:00.348
The tide of the war will greatly turn in our favor

00:03:00.598 --> 00:03:03.809
if we can maintain our hold on Boreas.

00:03:04.060 --> 00:03:04.977
Yes.

00:03:05.227 --> 00:03:08.773
Let us fight side by side until then!

00:03:09.023 --> 00:03:10.983
For the Augusta.

00:03:11.233 --> 00:03:15.154
To eliminate strife from this world.

00:03:15.404 --> 00:03:18.282
A witch's sister and a traitor, huh?

00:03:18.532 --> 00:03:20.451
--A perfect match.
--What?!

00:03:20.701 --> 00:03:22.536
You're obviously going to backstab us too.

00:03:22.620 --> 00:03:24.121
Stop, Magnolia.

00:03:24.372 --> 00:03:26.791
But...

00:03:27.041 --> 00:03:30.294
He's a trustworthy man, Dyan.

00:03:30.544 --> 00:03:32.630
Glacies has been destroyed.

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:38.094
All we can do now is fight
until vengeance is ours.

00:03:38.344 --> 00:03:41.055
Even at the cost of our lives.

00:03:42.098 --> 00:03:43.641
Dyan!

00:03:45.476 --> 00:03:46.977
Fam...

00:03:48.437 --> 00:03:50.231
Dyan! Are you hungry?!

00:03:50.481 --> 00:03:51.649
No, she isn't!

00:03:51.899 --> 00:03:53.776
Let's go, Dyan!

00:04:00.157 --> 00:04:03.244
I'm sorry. I'm not very hungry...

00:04:03.494 --> 00:04:07.581
I'll bring something nice to drink, then.

00:04:20.886 --> 00:04:22.346
Huh?

00:04:31.355 --> 00:04:32.356
Where's Dio?

00:04:32.606 --> 00:04:36.318
I, umm, looked away for
just a moment, and then...

00:04:36.569 --> 00:04:37.820
Sheesh!

00:04:38.070 --> 00:04:40.281
Sorry to impose like this!

00:04:41.657 --> 00:04:42.575
Dig?

00:04:42.825 --> 00:04:45.077
--Oh, Fam!
--S5r5!

00:04:45.327 --> 00:04:49.039
I got hungry, so I went
scavenging, and then... Right?

00:04:49.290 --> 00:04:53.002
Yes. I was dining when this
gentleman introduced himself!

00:04:53.252 --> 00:04:56.797
Doesn't that mean he
interrupted your meal, then?

00:04:57.047 --> 00:05:00.217
Huh? Does it really...?

00:05:01.927 --> 00:05:03.929
I guess the Augusta has it rough too.

00:05:04.180 --> 00:05:08.142
Sire“! blames herself for
everyone fighting like this...

00:05:08.392 --> 00:05:13.606
And Millia's having a really hard time too,
being called a witch's sister...

00:05:13.856 --> 00:05:16.650
Oh, is she?

00:05:16.901 --> 00:05:19.278
Fam! Gisey! Orders to fall in!

00:05:21.280 --> 00:05:23.449
She's so much better all nice and light!

00:05:23.699 --> 00:05:26.160
We're just supposed to be lookouts? That's it?!

00:05:26.410 --> 00:05:30.289
We had it coming, after doin'
our own thing the other day!

00:05:40.758 --> 00:05:43.844
All right, Birdbrain, bring it on!

00:05:56.815 --> 00:06:01.946
General Kayv5n's 2nd Fleet has yet
to recover from the Glacies battle.

00:06:02.196 --> 00:06:05.741
But the Federation still has
Admiral Sadri's 1st Fleet,

00:06:05.991 --> 00:06:08.494
which remains nearly unscathed.

00:06:08.744 --> 00:06:12.164
This fortress will not fall.

00:06:12.414 --> 00:06:18.420
Not as long as it is protected by
its thick mist and deep crevasses...

00:06:18.671 --> 00:06:20.214
The fortress may be impenetrable,

00:06:20.464 --> 00:06:24.468
but what if something
happens inside it, among us?!

00:06:24.718 --> 00:06:29.598
Are you referring to the hard feelings
between Glacies and (Yang's squad?

00:06:29.848 --> 00:06:35.604
Or is it that you don't fully trust in
your own abilities as a commander?

00:06:40.109 --> 00:06:44.154
Soldiers aren't the only ones who grow
strong in battle; commanders do too.

00:06:44.405 --> 00:06:47.741
Just as the soldiers of Turan will, so will you.

00:06:47.992 --> 00:06:49.618
General...

00:06:49.868 --> 00:06:53.747
We have justice and the Augusta on our side.

00:06:56.667 --> 00:06:58.794
1 and 2 o'clock, all clear!

00:06:59.044 --> 00:07:01.255
10 o'clock, all clear.

00:07:01.505 --> 00:07:03.507
360 degrees!

00:07:03.757 --> 00:07:07.970
Nothing but water and sky and clouds!

00:07:14.018 --> 00:07:16.103
It's so pretty...

00:07:16.353 --> 00:07:19.523
The Grand Lake is so beautiful...

00:07:19.773 --> 00:07:22.276
Why does there have to be a war?

00:07:22.526 --> 00:07:27.072
Yeah. If it weren't for this war,
Millia and Dyan would still...

00:07:29.491 --> 00:07:31.493
--Gisey?!
--I'm fine!

00:07:35.789 --> 00:07:38.375
They're flocking so wildly...!

00:07:38.626 --> 00:07:41.420
There's something above
the horizon at 11 o'clock!

00:07:41.670 --> 00:07:42.546
Muffle our sound!

00:07:42.796 --> 00:07:45.841
Roger! Target at 11 o'clock! Altitude, 250!

00:07:49.553 --> 00:07:54.391
70 Grouse Super-dreadnoughts
and 80 Kishar Dreadnoughts.

00:07:54.642 --> 00:07:55.893
Gisey.

00:07:56.143 --> 00:07:58.103
The Federation's 1st Fleet.

00:07:58.354 --> 00:08:01.273
Boreas patrol ships detected.
Scrambling interceptors!

00:08:01.523 --> 00:08:03.275
Let them go.

00:08:03.525 --> 00:08:06.487
Let them report about the scale of our fleet.

00:08:06.737 --> 00:08:08.614
Will the enemy take action?

00:08:08.864 --> 00:08:13.535
Vasant's earnestness comes from
supporting those above her.

00:08:13.786 --> 00:08:17.081
Her rag-tag army will be far too
intoxicated from its first victory in battle;

00:08:17.331 --> 00:08:20.417
she'll be unable to keep it in check.

00:08:20.668 --> 00:08:22.711
There's no better time to fight than now!

00:08:22.961 --> 00:08:24.963
It's just an old man and his 1st Fleet!

00:08:25.214 --> 00:08:29.551
Yeah! We have General firang
and his 3rd Fleet on our side now!

00:08:37.851 --> 00:08:40.020
C_)rang.

00:08:40.270 --> 00:08:43.691
I also feel that holding
our ground would be best.

00:08:45.943 --> 00:08:50.155
I'm glad to have you as part
of the Joint Forces now.

00:08:50.406 --> 00:08:52.157
For Augusta Sire-l.

00:08:53.992 --> 00:08:56.286
Gloria, Augusta.

00:09:17.725 --> 00:09:20.853
Is there going to be more fighting again?

00:09:22.646 --> 00:09:24.064
Good tailwinds!

00:09:24.314 --> 00:09:25.149
<i>F am?</i>

00:09:25.399 --> 00:09:26.859
Don't die out there, Dyan.

00:09:27.109 --> 00:09:29.820
You have to make up with
Millia when you get back!

00:09:30.070 --> 00:09:31.572
You too, Magnolia!

00:09:31.822 --> 00:09:33.741
See you later!

00:09:34.908 --> 00:09:35.993
Shall I translate?

00:09:36.243 --> 00:09:38.245
No. Let's go.

00:09:38.495 --> 00:09:39.997
Rogen

00:09:48.964 --> 00:09:50.591
Fam...

00:09:54.595 --> 00:09:58.265
Just when the Exile's about to return, too...

00:10:04.688 --> 00:10:07.024
Glacies squad approaching from the rear!

00:10:07.274 --> 00:10:08.859
Total ships, 50!

00:10:09.109 --> 00:10:10.778
Glacies, huh...?

00:10:13.405 --> 00:10:15.866
The 3rd Fleet...

00:10:16.116 --> 00:10:19.077
Commander to all units.

00:10:20.621 --> 00:10:25.083
Our targets are the Federation
1st Fleet's Vanship carriers.

00:10:25.334 --> 00:10:29.880
Command ship to all units.
Our target is the Federation's 1st Fleet...

00:10:30.130 --> 00:10:34.426
Specifically, the Maguilitars
and lmperium Vanship carriers.

00:10:38.096 --> 00:10:40.516
Glacies squad now passing overhead!

00:10:53.570 --> 00:10:57.533
The Maguilitars has been hit!
Unable to launch Vanship squadrons!

00:11:03.872 --> 00:11:05.290
The lmperius has been downed!

00:11:05.541 --> 00:11:06.625
--General?!
--Second Glacies wave incoming!

00:11:06.875 --> 00:11:07.876
--Let them have air superiority.
--Second Glacies wave incoming!

00:11:08.126 --> 00:11:08.877
--Let them have air superiority.
--20 ships!

00:11:09.127 --> 00:11:10.462
--It is fleet strength that will decide
--20 ships!

00:11:10.712 --> 00:11:12.464
The victor of this battle.

00:11:16.009 --> 00:11:18.470
Glacies squad's preemptive
assault was a success!

00:11:18.720 --> 00:11:20.639
No enemy ships in sight!

00:11:20.889 --> 00:11:22.766
Air superiority is now ours!

00:11:23.016 --> 00:11:24.476
Yes.

00:11:27.187 --> 00:11:28.730
Transmit the signal!

00:11:30.190 --> 00:11:31.567
A signal from the Borth?

00:11:31.817 --> 00:11:33.735
Reconciliation?

00:11:33.986 --> 00:11:36.905
"Attention, 3rd Fleet..."

00:11:37.155 --> 00:11:41.243
"Attack rebel forces from the rear
as per prearranged pincer operation!"

00:11:41.493 --> 00:11:42.536
Pincer operation?!

00:11:42.786 --> 00:11:45.330
Curse Admiral Sadri's craftiness...!

00:11:47.791 --> 00:11:51.253
A pincer attack?! They're up
to their treachery again!

00:11:51.503 --> 00:11:52.963
Please let us have revenge!

00:11:53.046 --> 00:11:55.340
<i>N!
ya“?</i>

00:11:55.424 --> 00:12:00.012
Wait. We don't know yet that
the 3rd Fleet is our enemy.

00:12:02.681 --> 00:12:03.932
Incoming Glacies squadron!

00:12:04.182 --> 00:12:06.184
They're hostile! We'll be
killed if we don't shoot first!

00:12:06.435 --> 00:12:08.770
Fire! Shoot them down!

00:12:24.953 --> 00:12:27.664
Treachery confirmed.

00:12:27.915 --> 00:12:31.335
Annihilate our enemy, the 3rd Fleet!

00:12:31.585 --> 00:12:33.045
R°gefl

00:12:34.129 --> 00:12:35.339
Glacies, incoming fast!

00:12:35.589 --> 00:12:38.425
Fire! Fire! Shoot them down!

00:12:50.312 --> 00:12:53.106
The lmpulsus has been downed!
Glacies is hostile!

00:12:53.357 --> 00:12:55.025
--Barrage fire!
--Belay that!

00:12:55.275 --> 00:12:57.152
Dyan! Don't!

00:13:05.702 --> 00:13:10.290
--...#5, #7, and #11 hit!
--Don't fire! Glacies is not our enemy!

00:13:10.540 --> 00:13:12.209
...have all caught fire!

00:13:16.046 --> 00:13:18.048
The 3rd Fleet...!

00:13:22.010 --> 00:13:23.470
Grant us...

00:13:25.055 --> 00:13:26.765
...the power of the Priestesses.

00:13:26.848 --> 00:13:28.433
Don't shoot!

00:13:38.902 --> 00:13:41.613
Fifteen ally ships damaged or downed!

00:13:41.863 --> 00:13:45.075
The enemy strategy has led
to confusion and friendly fire!

00:13:45.325 --> 00:13:48.829
It's insane! So many ships have been shot down!

00:13:52.457 --> 00:13:54.668
How many ships have returned?

00:13:54.918 --> 00:13:56.253
Fifteen.

00:13:56.503 --> 00:13:58.088
We leave at once.

00:13:58.338 --> 00:13:59.756
Fuel up halfway...

00:14:00.007 --> 00:14:03.218
...and load as many anti-ship shells as possible.

00:14:03.301 --> 00:14:04.761
Dyan!

00:14:09.433 --> 00:14:11.560
Why did you interfere?!

00:14:11.643 --> 00:14:14.563
You can't shoot your allies...!

00:14:14.646 --> 00:14:19.526
So many of my comrades just died!
All because I was naive!

00:14:19.609 --> 00:14:21.486
St°I°, Dyan!

00:14:21.737 --> 00:14:23.739
The Jagannath never fired!

00:14:23.989 --> 00:14:27.534
It never fired back, even after you shot it up!

00:14:27.617 --> 00:14:30.871
She says the Jagannath never once fired back.

00:14:31.121 --> 00:14:33.165
I'm well aware of that!

00:14:46.928 --> 00:14:49.181
--Retreat?!
--Dio!

00:14:55.896 --> 00:14:59.775
Lend the 3rd Fleet support! Focus on
maintaining allied military might!

00:15:00.025 --> 00:15:02.486
We will bring up the rear!

00:15:02.736 --> 00:15:06.531
Buy time until the Turan fleet has withdrawn!

00:15:08.742 --> 00:15:12.329
Portside engine chamber
badly damaged! Speed down 50%!

00:15:12.579 --> 00:15:13.789
Captain! We need to abandon ship!

00:15:14.039 --> 00:15:17.375
No, not yet! We must get
Princess Millia back to Boreas!

00:15:22.589 --> 00:15:24.091
The Jagannath...!

00:15:27.719 --> 00:15:30.097
Portside propellers and engine chamber hit!

00:15:30.347 --> 00:15:32.265
Damage to liquid Claudia conduits!

00:15:32.516 --> 00:15:33.683
Seal off damaged areas!

00:15:33.934 --> 00:15:36.686
Reroute all remaining conduits
and maintain speed!

00:15:36.937 --> 00:15:38.605
Don't give up!

00:15:46.822 --> 00:15:50.325
Our real enemy is the 1st Fleet!

00:15:50.575 --> 00:15:52.035
Fire!

00:15:53.662 --> 00:15:57.332
Princess Millia! You must abandon ship!
This ship is done for!

00:15:59.000 --> 00:16:01.169
That is not the Anshar;

00:16:01.419 --> 00:16:04.881
it is Princess Millia's command ship,
the Lasas, and we will show no mercy!

00:16:05.132 --> 00:16:06.633
Cut off her retreat!

00:16:06.883 --> 00:16:10.804
And destroy the entire
bothersome 3rd Fleet as well!

00:16:11.054 --> 00:16:13.056
Boreas grows near!

00:16:21.690 --> 00:16:23.567
There's just too many of them!

00:16:23.817 --> 00:16:26.194
03, ammunition at zero.

00:16:26.444 --> 00:16:29.197
Enemy losses only at 5%.

00:16:29.447 --> 00:16:32.659
07, ammunition at zero.

00:16:32.909 --> 00:16:36.121
51, ammunition at zero.

00:16:44.546 --> 00:16:45.380
What's happening?!

00:16:45.630 --> 00:16:48.258
--Lookouts!
--The Aniguis has been downed!

00:16:56.975 --> 00:16:59.603
Sorry for the wait. We've come to get you.

00:16:59.853 --> 00:17:01.188
The Silvius!

00:17:01.438 --> 00:17:03.064
The Reaper...!

00:17:04.357 --> 00:17:05.817
Fire everything!

00:17:22.167 --> 00:17:23.960
Princess Millia!

00:17:24.211 --> 00:17:25.045
Teddy!

00:17:25.295 --> 00:17:27.839
Thank goodness! Oh, thank goodness!

00:17:29.049 --> 00:17:31.551
Princess...!

00:17:31.801 --> 00:17:33.637
What a relief.

00:17:33.887 --> 00:17:36.723
I'm glad you're all okay.

00:17:36.973 --> 00:17:43.271
I'm sorry it took so long; we had
to repair the Silvius while in hiding.

00:17:43.521 --> 00:17:45.565
I'm just glad you're all right!

00:17:46.608 --> 00:17:48.068
Where's Fam?

00:17:50.111 --> 00:17:51.947
--Time to fly, Fam!
--Dio! Your arm...!

00:17:52.197 --> 00:17:54.199
It hurts!

00:18:11.007 --> 00:18:12.717
What was that?!

00:18:12.968 --> 00:18:15.887
The rock wharf's been blown up!

00:18:16.137 --> 00:18:19.766
The rubble is filling in the southern crevasse!

00:18:20.016 --> 00:18:21.476
That can't be!

00:18:25.230 --> 00:18:26.439
Princess...

00:18:26.690 --> 00:18:28.108
Come with me, Teddy.

00:18:28.358 --> 00:18:30.318
Yes, Princess!

00:18:30.568 --> 00:18:32.195
Séré!

00:18:32.445 --> 00:18:34.906
Let's stop this fighting!

00:18:35.156 --> 00:18:36.449
Fam...

00:18:36.700 --> 00:18:38.702
Not being able to trust your own friends...

00:18:38.952 --> 00:18:41.371
That's not right at all. So...!

00:18:41.621 --> 00:18:45.125
I want to end it too!
I don't like everyone fighting!

00:18:45.375 --> 00:18:47.669
How can we stop it?!

00:18:47.919 --> 00:18:51.756
If anyone can stop it, you can, Augusta Sire-l.

00:18:57.178 --> 00:18:58.555
The collapse of the cliff face

00:18:58.805 --> 00:19:01.308
has eliminated the southern
Boreas corridor's altitude ceiling!

00:19:01.558 --> 00:19:03.768
We can now advance!

00:19:04.019 --> 00:19:07.063
Bring down Boreas! Vanguard ships, charge!

00:19:08.106 --> 00:19:09.232
Vanguard, charge!

00:19:09.482 --> 00:19:10.775
Charge!

00:19:11.026 --> 00:19:13.862
Enemy vanguard has
breached last line of defense!

00:19:14.112 --> 00:19:15.447
Prepare for hand-to-hand combat!

00:19:15.697 --> 00:19:17.824
Take the Augusta to a safe location!

00:19:24.205 --> 00:19:26.124
To Vasant and Sadri...

00:19:26.374 --> 00:19:29.127
--Without fail.
--Leave it to us!

00:19:31.087 --> 00:19:32.839
Princess Millia!

00:19:37.302 --> 00:19:40.263
--Gisey!
--All ready to go!

00:19:41.306 --> 00:19:42.515
Here goes...

00:19:42.766 --> 00:19:45.268
Y-Yes, Princess!

00:19:52.359 --> 00:19:55.403
An envoy? In this situation?

00:19:55.653 --> 00:19:58.198
Wait! Wait, Dyan!

00:19:59.366 --> 00:20:00.825
<i>F am?</i>

00:20:04.829 --> 00:20:09.501
Target the upper command center
and the artillery batteries!

00:20:12.462 --> 00:20:13.546
They've made it this far?!

00:20:13.797 --> 00:20:15.757
Let's punch through, Gisey!

00:20:20.637 --> 00:20:23.640
Attention, Sky Pirates! Turn back at once!

00:20:23.890 --> 00:20:26.559
Do so or you will be shot down!

00:20:41.825 --> 00:20:45.537
Stop, Dyan! We have to
deliver the Augusta's letter!

00:20:45.787 --> 00:20:47.247
Dyan!

00:20:47.330 --> 00:20:50.291
I refuse to allow a truce!

00:20:51.334 --> 00:20:52.961
They're going to shoot!

00:20:59.717 --> 00:21:01.261
They disappeared!

00:21:02.595 --> 00:21:04.264
They broke free from me?

00:21:04.347 --> 00:21:06.474
<i>Dy an'?</i>

00:21:06.558 --> 00:21:09.269
With such a tiny Vanship...?

00:21:24.367 --> 00:21:27.662
A missive from Augusta Sire-l.

00:21:27.912 --> 00:21:34.752
It pains Sire“! greatly, seeing you
fight each other like this!

00:21:35.003 --> 00:21:36.629
Augusta Sari...

00:21:36.880 --> 00:21:39.799
The Augusta desires peace.

00:21:40.049 --> 00:21:42.469
She asks for an immediate truce, General.

00:21:42.719 --> 00:21:45.013
The Augusta...

00:21:45.263 --> 00:21:48.558
It was for her sake that I...

00:21:48.808 --> 00:21:51.603
That I turned on that treacherous Luscinia!

00:21:56.483 --> 00:21:58.526
Augusta...

00:22:01.070 --> 00:22:05.700
Inform everyone to cease
the assault on Boreas at once.

00:22:05.950 --> 00:22:07.744
General?!

00:22:07.994 --> 00:22:12.290
The Augusta- Lady Sir?!“ wishes for a truce.

00:22:13.708 --> 00:22:15.627
__Fam!

00:22:15.877 --> 00:22:17.378
We did it!

00:22:17.629 --> 00:22:19.631
It's over! It's over!

00:22:19.881 --> 00:22:22.467
The war is over!

00:22:24.511 --> 00:22:26.721
We did it!

00:22:31.476 --> 00:22:32.977
Rahin.

00:24:03.234 --> 00:24:04.319
<i>You must've had a hard time!</i>

00:24:04.569 --> 00:24:08.031
<i>Yes! But I knew I'd see you again someday,
so I conducted training every day!</i>

00:24:08.281 --> 00:24:10.158
<i>--What kind of training?
"Making your favorite royal milk tea...</i>

00:24:10.408 --> 00:24:12.327
<i>...with just the right strength!</i>

00:24:12.577 --> 00:24:14.495
--Huh?
--Baking your favorite raisin scones...

00:24:14.746 --> 00:24:16.789
<i>...in just the right amount!</i>

00:24:17.040 --> 00:24:18.666
<i>Teddy! You didn't need to train for--</i>

00:24:18.916 --> 00:24:22.587
<i>The entire Silvius maintenance crew
has mastered these things now!</i>

00:24:22.837 --> 00:24:24.631
<i>What?! You mean you trained them?!</i>

00:24:24.881 --> 00:24:27.300
<i>Princess Millia!</i>
